.TH TACON 1 "February 2026" "tacon 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tacon \- TACACS+ client CLI for authentication, authorization, and accounting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tacon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-server\-addr\fR \fIHOST:PORT\fR
\fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tacon
is a command-line TACACS+ client for authentication, authorization, and accounting (AAA) operations. It supports both traditional TACACS+ with obfuscation and modern TACACS+ over TLS 1.3, making it suitable for both legacy and next-generation network infrastructure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server\-addr " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
IP address and port of the TACACS+ server (e.g., "192.168.1.1:49"). This option is required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-obfuscation\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Obfuscation key (shared secret) for encrypting TACACS+ messages.
.TP
.BR \-\-use\-tls
Use TLS 1.3 for the connection to the TACACS+ server.
.TP
.BR \-\-client\-certificate " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to client certificate file for TLS authentication.
.TP
.BR \-\-client\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to client private key file for TLS authentication.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity level. Can be specified multiple times:
.RS
.IP "\-v" 10
Warning level
.IP "\-vv"
Info level
.IP "\-vvv"
Debug level
.IP "\-vvvv"
Trace level
.RE
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B accounting
Send an accounting record to the TACACS+ server.
.TP
.B authentication
Perform authentication against the TACACS+ server (not yet implemented).
.TP
.B authorization
Perform authorization check against the TACACS+ server (not yet implemented).
.TP
.B batch
Run in batch mode using commands from a JSON file.
.TP
.B help
Print help information for a specific command.
.SH ACCOUNTING COMMAND
.PP
Record command execution to the TACACS+ server:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tacon \-s 192.168.1.1:49 \-k "secret" accounting \\
    \-\-user admin \\
    \-\-port tty0 \\
    \-\-rem\-addr 10.0.0.100 \\
    "show running\-config"
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Accounting Options:
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Username for the request.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port identifier (e.g., "tty0", "console").
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rem\-addr " " \fIADDR\fR
Remote address of the client.
.TP
.BR \-\-custom\-flag\-1
Set TAC_PLUS_CUSTOM_FLAG_1 (0x40) on packet header.
.TP
.BR \-\-custom\-flag\-2
Set TAC_PLUS_CUSTOM_FLAG_2 (0x80) on packet header.
.TP
.BR \-\-session\-id " " \fIID\fR
Use a specific session ID instead of random.
.SH BATCH COMMAND
.PP
Execute multiple requests from a JSON file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tacon \-s 192.168.1.1:49 \-k "secret" batch requests.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Batch files use JSON format to define multiple TACACS+ requests with optional parallel execution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Traditional TACACS+ with Obfuscation:
.nf
tacon \\
    \-\-server\-addr tacacsserver.local:49 \\
    \-\-obfuscation\-key "tac_plus_key" \\
    \-\-user testuser \\
    \-\-port tty1 \\
    \-\-rem\-addr 192.168.1.100 \\
    \-vvv \\
    accounting "show version"
.fi
.TP
.B TACACS+ over TLS 1.3:
.nf
tacon \\
    \-\-server\-addr tacacsserver.local:449 \\
    \-\-use\-tls \\
    \-\-client\-certificate /path/to/client.crt \\
    \-\-client\-key /path/to/client.key \\
    \-\-user testuser \\
    \-\-port tty1 \\
    \-\-rem\-addr 192.168.1.100 \\
    accounting "show interfaces"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (connection failure, invalid arguments, or request failure)
